{
  "_sheet": "materials",
  "_doc": "One row per surface material the course and terrain use. albedo/normal/weather are content.json ids; uv_scale is metres per texture tile. Course.gd draws every textured row with one weathering shader: weather is a second texture mixed in by noise over weather_cover of the surface, grime is the strength of dirt streaks running down from a ramp's top edge (and its chipped lip), detail is the close-up detail overlay that keeps the texture sharp under the player. filter: aniso = mipmapped anisotropic (every shader material samples this way since world_r1). panel: cast slab size in metres on ramp faces (dark joints, a tone per slab; 0 = none); tint: albedo multiplier; crease_ao: how much the foot of a ramp face (the valley crease) is darkened and occluded. leaks: strength of Rust's dirt_stains_leaks drip decals hanging from a ramp face's top edge; debris: strength of the same atlas's gravel/litter band along the foot of a face (the crease of a valley); course.json weathering says which atlas bands. 0 turns either off. normal_depth: strength of the normal map on the course shader (1 = as Rust ships it; higher deepens the slab seams, cracks and pitting under a low sun).",
